theorem.content:
\label{Th:Main1-Existence}
Suppose that (G1)--(G5) are satisfied. 
\begin{enumerate}
\item[(a)] There exists a nontrivial solution $u_0 \in X^1 (\mathbb{R}^N)$ of \eqref{eq:main} that satisfies the Poho\v{z}aev constraint ${\mathcal M}$. 
\item[(b)] $u_0$ is a minimizer of the energy functional $J$ on ${\mathcal M}$.
\item[(c)] Every solution $u\in X^1(\mathbb{R}^N)$ of \eqref{eq:main} belongs to $C^{1,\alpha}_{\mathrm{loc}} (\mathbb{R}^N \setminus \{0\})$ for some $\alpha \in (0,1)$.
\item[(d)] If, in addition, $g$ is H\"older continuous, every solution $u\in X^1(\mathbb{R}^N)$ of \eqref{eq:main} is of the class $C^2 (\mathbb{R}^N\setminus \{0\})$.
\item[(e)] If, in addition, $g$ is odd, there exists a nontrivial, nonnegative, radial and radially nonincreasing solution in $X^1 (\mathbb{R}^N) \cap C^2 (\mathbb{R}^N \setminus \{0\})$ of \eqref{eq:main}, which is a minimizer of $J$ on ${\mathcal M}$.
\item[(f)] Every nonnegative solution of \eqref{eq:main} in $X^1(\mathbb{R}^N) \cap C^2 (\mathbb{R}^N \setminus\{0\})$ does not belong to $H^1 (\mathbb{R}^N)$.
\end{enumerate}

